@meta (title: "Explore a documentation review", locale: "en-US")

# Explore a documentation review

These fictional observations describe four chapters. Filter the chapters to
compare recorded review time; the summary, figure, and table share the same rows.

@toggle include_drafts = false (label: "Include draft chapters")
@slider minimum = 0 (min: 0, max: 40, step: 5, label: "Minimum review minutes")

@data reviews
chapter:text | minutes:number | approved:boolean
Setup | 10 | true
Editing | 20 | true
Exports | 30 | false
Reference | 40 | false
@end

@view visible = reviews (
  where: (include_drafts or row.approved) and row.minutes >= minimum,
  sort: "minutes",
)
@calc total = sum(visible, "minutes")
@calc average = if(count(visible) > 0, mean(visible, "minutes"), 0)

The selection contains **{{ count(visible) }} chapters** and
**{{ total }} minutes** of recorded review time.

@when count(visible) > 0
Average review time is **{{ fixed(average, 1) }} minutes per chapter**.
@end

@when count(visible) == 0
No chapters match. Lower the minimum or include drafts.
@end

@chart bar visible (
  x: "chapter",
  y: "minutes",
  title: "Review time for selected chapters",
  yLabel: "Minutes",
)

@table visible (title: "Selected review observations")

The sample is too small to establish a general reading-speed benchmark.
